## English Overview

### What is Veil-Evasion?
**Veil-Evasion** (part of the *Veil-Framework* suite) is an open-source offensive security tool specifically engineered to generate **Metasploit-compatible payloads** capable of bypassing common antivirus (AV) solutions. Instead of relying solely on standard MSFvenom encoders—which modern AV engines easily detect via static signatures—Veil dynamically wraps or encrypts shellcode inside newly compiled binaries written in diverse programming languages.

### Core Capabilities

| Feature | Technical Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Multi-Language Wrappers** | Encapsulates shellcode inside **Python, C, C#, Go, Ruby, or PowerShell** source code before compiling into a standalone `.exe`. |
| **Crypters & Obfuscation** | Applies custom **AES/XOR encryption** routines, variable randomization, and junk-code insertion to break static signature heuristics. |
| **Memory Injection** | Offers *VirtualAlloc* and direct memory-injection techniques so the payload executes straight in RAM without touching the disk. |
| **Metasploit Integration** | Automatically outputs matching `.rc` (resource) scripts to spin up the required `multi/handler` listener effortlessly. |

